# Line endings are pinned so a checkout is the same on every machine.
#
# This repository hashes its own files. benchmark/FREEZE_MANIFEST.json
# and benchmark/drills/MANIFEST.json record the sha256 of frozen
# material, and B001 fails the build when one moves. Those hashes were
# taken on LF content.
#
# Git's core.autocrlf=true, which a Windows install sets by default,
# rewrites text files to CRLF on the way into the working tree. Without
# this file, checking out the repository on Windows changes the bytes
# of 108 frozen files and every one of them reports as an unrecorded
# change to frozen material. Nothing was edited; the checkout did it.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to LF everywhere, so the freeze check
# reads the same bytes the manifest recorded. The hashers normalise
# line endings as well, so a tree that predates this file still
# verifies, but the two belong together: this makes the tree right and
# the hasher makes the check robust if it is ever wrong again.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF or cmd.exe mis-parses them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Hashed byte for byte, never transformed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
